--- a/HISTORY.md
+++ b/HISTORY.md
@@ -4,7 +4,12 @@ Release History
 dev
 ---
 
-- \[Short description of non-trivial change.\]
+**Improvements**
+- Added `Session.timeout`, a default timeout applied to every request sent
+  through the session (including redirects and direct `Session.send()` calls)
+  that does not pass its own `timeout`. A per-request `timeout=None` uses the
+  session default; pass `timeout=(None, None)` to disable the timeout for a
+  single request. Defaults to `None`, so existing behavior is unchanged.
 
 
 2.34.2 (2026-05-14)
diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
index f5209a5..f047733 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,22 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+When many requests go through one :class:`Session <requests.Session>`, set a
+default once with :attr:`Session.timeout <requests.Session.timeout>` instead of
+repeating ``timeout=`` on every call. It accepts the same values as the
+``timeout`` argument and applies to every request sent through the session,
+including redirects, unless that request passes its own ``timeout``::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    s.timeout = (3.05, 27)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')                 # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=60)     # this call only: 60
+
+As with other session settings, a per-request ``timeout=None`` means "not
+specified", so the session default still applies. To wait forever on a single
+request despite a session default, pass ``timeout=(None, None)``.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
